Package: y-not
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6, libacl1, libcap2, libselinux1
Maintainer: Elena Frison <e_gavrilova_frison@zohomail.eu>
Homepage: https://github.com/ElenaFri/y-not
Description: explain why a user can or cannot access a file or directory
 y-not traces the access path to a file and reports whether a given user
 can read, write, or execute it, and if not, which component of the path
 blocks access and why (owner/group/other permissions, supplementary
 groups, POSIX ACLs, Linux capabilities, symlinks and special files).
